{\pard\sa160\sb160\b\fs28 3. Scope & High-Level Functional Requirements\b0\par}

{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Customer portal web app (React) with responsive UI for mobile (~50% usage assumption).\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Authentication: TOTP-based login; session management with secure cookies or tokens; reasonable expiration and refresh.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Authorization: strict access control—each user can only access their proposals.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Proposal viewing: display proposal details (system configuration, savings, sales pitch content).\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab PDF export: in-browser export of exactly what user sees (or server-generated equivalent if needed).\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Auditability: log access to proposals (who/when) for sales visibility and compliance.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Admin/system integration: pull proposals created in the existing sales system; keep customer portal read-only for v1 (except auth/session state).\par}

{\pard\sa160\sb160\b\fs28 4. Proposed Architecture (v1)\b0\par}

{\pard\sa120\fs22 We will introduce a new standalone Customer Portal consisting of: (1) React frontend, (2) Node.js/TypeScript API, (3) PostgreSQL tables for portal identity + proposal metadata, (4) object storage for proposal assets, and (5) CI/CD + IaC for repeatable deployments.\par}

{\pard\sa120\sb120\b\fs24 4.1 Components\b0\par}

{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Customer Portal Frontend: React-based web app (responsive) served via CDN/static hosting.\par}
