{\pard\sa160\sb160\b\fs28 5. Authentication & Authorization Design\b0\par}

{\pard\sa120\sb120\b\fs24 5.1 TOTP approach (v1)\b0\par}

{\pard\sa120\fs22 TOTP normally requires a shared secret provisioned into an authenticator app. For a lead/customer portal, we must define an enrollment path and an identifier. Given the requirements, we propose email-first enrollment with a one-time magic link to bootstrap TOTP enrollment, then TOTP for subsequent logins.\par}

{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Bootstrap: send email magic link (or SMS) once to verify ownership of identifier, then enroll TOTP (QR code) and store encrypted secret.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Login: user provides identifier + TOTP code.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Secret storage: encrypt TOTP secrets with KMS-managed key (or envelope encryption) before storing in PostgreSQL.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Rate limiting: per IP + per identifier; lockout/backoff on repeated failures.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Future extensibility: auth_identities table supports OAuth identities without schema changes.\par}

{\pard\sa120\sb120\b\fs24 5.2 Sessions (cookies vs tokens)\b0\par}

{\pard\sa120\fs22 Use secure, httpOnly, sameSite cookies carrying an opaque session id (recommended for browser apps) OR a short-lived JWT with refresh via secure cookie. For speed and simplicity in v1, use opaque sessions stored server-side (PostgreSQL or Redis).\par}

{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Cookie: httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax/Strict (evaluate cross-domain needs).\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Session duration: 7–14 days sliding expiration; absolute max 30 days (adjustable).\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Revocation: server-side session store allows immediate logout/revocation.\par}

{\pard\sa120\sb120\b\fs24 5.3 Access control\b0\par}

{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab All proposal queries must be scoped by authenticated customer_id (no direct access by proposal id alone).\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Row-level checks enforced in API layer; optionally add PostgreSQL RLS for defense-in-depth.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab S3 access via pre-signed URLs only after authorization; short TTL (e.g., 60–300 seconds).\par}

{\pard\sa160\sb160\b\fs28 6. Proposal Rendering & In-Browser PDF Export\b0\par}

{\pard\sa120\sb120\b\fs24 6.1 Rendering strategy\b0\par}

{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Preferred: render proposal from structured data (JSON) into React components; consistent UX and supports future interactive features.\par}
{\pard\li360\sa80\fs22 \bullet\tab Fallback: if only PDF exists today, render PDF in-browser (pdf.js) and allow export/download; interactive features will require structured data later.\par}
